      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T12:06:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we reject `ring_size \u003d\u003d 0` in `sfdp_session_stats_ring_init()` so every caller is protected? The CLI accepts `size 0`; the next export reserves against a zero-sized ring and ring commit performs modulo zero, potentially crashing VPP. An upper-bound/overflow check would also prevent invalid ring allocations.",
      "revId": "67d00741edcb696d9fd146d418ba251d652e0f31",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f43796ff_868e9113",
        "filename": "src/plugins/sfdp_services/session_stats/cli.c",
        "patchSetId": 34
      },
      "lineNbr": 129,
      "author": {
        "id": 3027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-25T14:22:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure. The current behavior is to only protect through the API call, but no the CLI call to configure a ring buffer.\n\nI\u0027ve added an explicit check in `sfdp_session_stats_ring_init()` for `ring_size \u003d\u003d 0` and a negative API test case when we attempt to configure a ring buffer with size zero.",
      "parentUuid": "02cc598d_29c91a91",
      "revId": "67d00741edcb696d9fd146d418ba251d652e0f31",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b188774_f6fa6b45",
        "filename": "src/plugins/sfdp_services/session_stats/node.c",
        "patchSetId": 34
      },
      "lineNbr": 67,
