        "id": 361
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-17T12:06:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we locate TCP using the L4 offset computed by the SFDP parser and validate the header bounds? Adding fixed IPv4/IPv6 header sizes interprets IPv4 options or IPv6 extension headers as TCP, producing invalid TCP/RTT statistics and potentially reading beyond the valid header.",
      "revId": "67d00741edcb696d9fd146d418ba251d652e0f31",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1f4933fe_6bf865e1",
        "filename": "src/plugins/sfdp_services/session_stats/node.c",
        "patchSetId": 34
      },
      "lineNbr": 67,
      "author": {
        "id": 3027
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-08-25T14:22:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added additional checks for the TCP header, which should address use-cases where IPV4 options or IPv6 option headers are present.\n\nIt seems like we currently don\u0027t have overall tests in SFDP for packets with IPv4 options or IPv6 extension headers, and these should be investigated in a subsequent patch.",
      "parentUuid": "0b188774_f6fa6b45",
      "revId": "67d00741edcb696d9fd146d418ba251d652e0f31",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
    {
